<p><b>Artificial intelligence</b> (<b>AI</b>) is the capability of <a href=
=3D"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Computer" title=3D"Computer">computationa=
l systems</a> to perform tasks typically associated with <a href=3D"https:/=
/en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Human_intelligence" title=3D"Human intelligence">hum=
an intelligence</a>, such as <a href=3D"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Learn=
ing" title=3D"Learning">learning</a>, <a href=3D"https://en.wikipedia.org/w=
iki/Reason" title=3D"Reason">reasoning</a>, <a href=3D"https://en.wikipedia=
.org/wiki/Problem-solving" class=3D"mw-redirect" title=3D"Problem-solving">=
problem-solving</a>, <a href=3D"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Perception" t=
itle=3D"Perception">perception</a>, and <a href=3D"https://en.wikipedia.org=
/wiki/Decision-making" title=3D"Decision-making">decision-making</a>. It is=
 a <a href=3D"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Field_of_research" class=3D"mw-=
redirect" title=3D"Field of research">field of research</a> in <a href=3D"h=
ttps://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Computer_science" title=3D"Computer science">c=
omputer science</a> that develops and studies methods and <a href=3D"https:=
//en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Software" title=3D"Software">software</a> systems t=
hat enable computational systems to perceive their environment and use <a h=
ref=3D"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Machine_learning" title=3D"Machine lea=
rning">learning</a> and <a href=3D"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Intelligen=
ce" title=3D"Intelligence">intelligence</a> to take actions that maximize t=
heir chances of achieving defined goals.<sup id=3D"cite_ref-FOOTNOTERussell=
Norvig20211=E2=80=934_1-0" class=3D"reference"><a href=3D"https://en.wikipe=
dia.org/wiki/Artificial_intelligence#cite_note-FOOTNOTERussellNorvig20211%E=
2%80%934-1"><span class=3D"cite-bracket">[</span>1<span class=3D"cite-brack=
et">]</span></a></sup>
</p><p>High-profile <a href=3D"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Applications_o=
f_AI" class=3D"mw-redirect" title=3D"Applications of AI">applications of AI=
</a> include advanced <a href=3D"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Web_search_e=
ngine" class=3D"mw-redirect" title=3D"Web search engine">web search engines=
</a> (e.g., <a href=3D"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Google_Search" title=
=3D"Google Search">Google Search</a>); <a href=3D"https://en.wikipedia.org/=
wiki/Recommendation_systems" class=3D"mw-redirect" title=3D"Recommendation =
systems">recommendation systems</a> (used by <a href=3D"https://en.wikipedi=
a.org/wiki/YouTube" title=3D"YouTube">YouTube</a>, <a href=3D"https://en.wi=
kipedia.org/wiki/Amazon_(company)" title=3D"Amazon (company)">Amazon</a>, a=
nd <a href=3D"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Netflix" title=3D"Netflix">Netf=
lix</a>); <a href=3D"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Virtual_assistant" title=
=3D"Virtual assistant">virtual assistants</a> (e.g., <a href=3D"https://en.=
wikipedia.org/wiki/Google_Assistant" title=3D"Google Assistant">Google Assi=
stant</a>, <a href=3D"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Siri" title=3D"Siri">Si=
ri</a>, and <a href=3D"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Amazon_Alexa" title=3D=
"Amazon Alexa">Alexa</a>); <a href=3D"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Autonom=
ous_vehicles" class=3D"mw-redirect" title=3D"Autonomous vehicles">autonomou=
s vehicles</a> (e.g., <a href=3D"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Waymo" title=
=3D"Waymo">Waymo</a>); <a href=3D"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Generative_=
artificial_intelligence" title=3D"Generative artificial intelligence">gener=
ative</a> and <a href=3D"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Computational_creati=
vity" title=3D"Computational creativity">creative</a> tools (e.g., <a href=
=3D"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Language_model" title=3D"Language model">=
language models</a> and <a href=3D"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/AI_art" cl=
ass=3D"mw-redirect" title=3D"AI art">AI art</a>); and <a href=3D"https://en=
.wikipedia.org/wiki/Superintelligence" title=3D"Superintelligence">superhum=
an</a> play and analysis in <a href=3D"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Strate=
gy_game" title=3D"Strategy game">strategy games</a> (e.g., <a href=3D"https=
://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Chess" title=3D"Chess">chess</a> and <a href=3D"ht=
tps://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Go_(game)" title=3D"Go (game)">Go</a>). However=
, many AI applications are not perceived as AI: "A lot of cutting edge AI h=
as filtered into general applications, often without being called AI becaus=
e once something becomes useful enough and common enough it's <a href=3D"ht=
tps://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/AI_effect" title=3D"AI effect">not labeled AI a=
nymore</a>."<sup id=3D"cite_ref-2" class=3D"reference"><a href=3D"https://e=
n.wikipedia.org/wiki/Artificial_intelligence#cite_note-2"><span class=3D"ci=
te-bracket">[</span>2<span class=3D"cite-bracket">]</span></a></sup><sup id=
=3D"cite_ref-3" class=3D"reference"><a href=3D"https://en.wikipedia.org/wik=
i/Artificial_intelligence#cite_note-3"><span class=3D"cite-bracket">[</span=
>3<span class=3D"cite-bracket">]</span></a></sup>
</p><p>Various subfields of AI research are centered around particular goal=
s and the use of particular tools. The traditional goals of AI research inc=
lude learning, <a href=3D"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Automated_reasoning=
" title=3D"Automated reasoning">reasoning</a>, <a href=3D"https://en.wikipe=
dia.org/wiki/Knowledge_representation" class=3D"mw-redirect" title=3D"Knowl=
edge representation">knowledge representation</a>, <a href=3D"https://en.wi=
kipedia.org/wiki/Automated_planning_and_scheduling" title=3D"Automated plan=
ning and scheduling">planning</a>, <a href=3D"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki=
/Natural_language_processing" title=3D"Natural language processing">natural=
 language processing</a>, <a href=3D"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Machine_=
perception" title=3D"Machine perception">perception</a>, and support for <a=
 href=3D"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Robotics" title=3D"Robotics">robotic=
s</a>.<sup id=3D"cite_ref-Problems_of_AI_4-0" class=3D"reference"><a href=
=3D"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Artificial_intelligence#cite_note-Problem=
s_of_AI-4"><span class=3D"cite-bracket">[</span>a<span class=3D"cite-bracke=
t">]</span></a></sup> To reach these goals, AI researchers have adapted and=
 integrated a wide range of techniques, including <a href=3D"https://en.wik=
ipedia.org/wiki/State_space_search" class=3D"mw-redirect" title=3D"State sp=
ace search">search</a> and <a href=3D"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mathema=
tical_optimization" title=3D"Mathematical optimization">mathematical optimi=
zation</a>, <a href=3D"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Formal_logic" class=3D=
"mw-redirect" title=3D"Formal logic">formal logic</a>, <a href=3D"https://e=
n.wikipedia.org/wiki/Artificial_neural_network" class=3D"mw-redirect" title=
=3D"Artificial neural network">artificial neural networks</a>, and methods =
based on <a href=3D"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Statistics" title=3D"Stat=
istics">statistics</a>, <a href=3D"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Operations=
_research" title=3D"Operations research">operations research</a>, and <a hr=
ef=3D"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Economics" title=3D"Economics">economic=
s</a>.<sup id=3D"cite_ref-Tools_of_AI_5-0" class=3D"reference"><a href=3D"h=
ttps://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Artificial_intelligence#cite_note-Tools_of_AI-=
5"><span class=3D"cite-bracket">[</span>b<span class=3D"cite-bracket">]</sp=
