le-width=3D"575" data-file-height=3D"325"></a><figcaption>A simple <a href=
=3D"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bayesian_network" title=3D"Bayesian netwo=
rk">Bayesian network</a>, with the associated <a href=3D"https://en.wikiped=
ia.org/wiki/Conditional_probability_table" title=3D"Conditional probability=
 table">conditional probability tables</a></figcaption></figure>
<p>Many problems in AI (including reasoning, planning, learning, perception=
, and robotics) require the agent to operate with incomplete or uncertain i=
nformation. AI researchers have devised a number of tools to solve these pr=
oblems using methods from <a href=3D"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Probabil=
ity" title=3D"Probability">probability</a> theory and economics.<sup id=3D"=
cite_ref-Stoch_93-0" class=3D"reference"><a href=3D"https://en.wikipedia.or=
g/wiki/Artificial_intelligence#cite_note-Stoch-93"><span class=3D"cite-brac=
ket">[</span>87<span class=3D"cite-bracket">]</span></a></sup> Precise math=
ematical tools have been developed that analyze how an agent can make choic=
es and plan, using <a href=3D"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Decision_theory=
" title=3D"Decision theory">decision theory</a>, <a href=3D"https://en.wiki=
pedia.org/wiki/Decision_analysis" title=3D"Decision analysis">decision anal=
ysis</a>,<sup id=3D"cite_ref-94" class=3D"reference"><a href=3D"https://en.=
wikipedia.org/wiki/Artificial_intelligence#cite_note-94"><span class=3D"cit=
e-bracket">[</span>88<span class=3D"cite-bracket">]</span></a></sup> and <a=
 href=3D"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Information_value_theory" class=3D"m=
w-redirect" title=3D"Information value theory">information value theory</a>=
.<sup id=3D"cite_ref-95" class=3D"reference"><a href=3D"https://en.wikipedi=
a.org/wiki/Artificial_intelligence#cite_note-95"><span class=3D"cite-bracke=
t">[</span>89<span class=3D"cite-bracket">]</span></a></sup> These tools in=
clude models such as <a href=3D"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Markov_decisi=
on_process" title=3D"Markov decision process">Markov decision processes</a>=
,<sup id=3D"cite_ref-96" class=3D"reference"><a href=3D"https://en.wikipedi=
a.org/wiki/Artificial_intelligence#cite_note-96"><span class=3D"cite-bracke=
t">[</span>90<span class=3D"cite-bracket">]</span></a></sup> dynamic <a hre=
f=3D"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Decision_network" class=3D"mw-redirect" =
title=3D"Decision network">decision networks</a>,<sup id=3D"cite_ref-Stocha=
stic_temporal_models_97-0" class=3D"reference"><a href=3D"https://en.wikipe=
dia.org/wiki/Artificial_intelligence#cite_note-Stochastic_temporal_models-9=
7"><span class=3D"cite-bracket">[</span>91<span class=3D"cite-bracket">]</s=
pan></a></sup> <a href=3D"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Game_theory" title=
=3D"Game theory">game theory</a> and <a href=3D"https://en.wikipedia.org/wi=
ki/Mechanism_design" title=3D"Mechanism design">mechanism design</a>.<sup i=
d=3D"cite_ref-98" class=3D"reference"><a href=3D"https://en.wikipedia.org/w=
iki/Artificial_intelligence#cite_note-98"><span class=3D"cite-bracket">[</s=
pan>92<span class=3D"cite-bracket">]</span></a></sup>
</p><p><a href=3D"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bayesian_network" title=3D"=
Bayesian network">Bayesian networks</a><sup id=3D"cite_ref-99" class=3D"ref=
erence"><a href=3D"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Artificial_intelligence#ci=
te_note-99"><span class=3D"cite-bracket">[</span>93<span class=3D"cite-brac=
ket">]</span></a></sup> are a tool that can be used for <a href=3D"https://=
en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Automated_reasoning" title=3D"Automated reasoning">re=
asoning</a> (using the <a href=3D"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bayesian_in=
ference" title=3D"Bayesian inference">Bayesian inference</a> algorithm),<su=
p id=3D"cite_ref-101" class=3D"reference"><a href=3D"https://en.wikipedia.o=
rg/wiki/Artificial_intelligence#cite_note-101"><span class=3D"cite-bracket"=
>[</span>g<span class=3D"cite-bracket">]</span></a></sup><sup id=3D"cite_re=
f-102" class=3D"reference"><a href=3D"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Artific=
ial_intelligence#cite_note-102"><span class=3D"cite-bracket">[</span>95<spa=
n class=3D"cite-bracket">]</span></a></sup> <a href=3D"https://en.wikipedia=
.org/wiki/Machine_learning" title=3D"Machine learning">learning</a> (using =
the <a href=3D"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Expectation%E2%80%93maximizati=
on_algorithm" title=3D"Expectation=E2=80=93maximization algorithm">expectat=
ion=E2=80=93maximization algorithm</a>),<sup id=3D"cite_ref-104" class=3D"r=
eference"><a href=3D"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Artificial_intelligence#=
cite_note-104"><span class=3D"cite-bracket">[</span>h<span class=3D"cite-br=
acket">]</span></a></sup><sup id=3D"cite_ref-105" class=3D"reference"><a hr=
