=3D"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Artificial_intelligence#cite_note-Stochas=
tic_temporal_models-97"><span class=3D"cite-bracket">[</span>91<span class=
=3D"cite-bracket">]</span></a></sup>
</p><p>Probabilistic algorithms can also be used for filtering, prediction,=
 smoothing, and finding explanations for streams of data, thus helping perc=
eption systems analyze processes that occur over time (e.g., <a href=3D"htt=
ps://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hidden_Markov_model" title=3D"Hidden Markov mode=
l">hidden Markov models</a> or <a href=3D"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kal=
man_filter" title=3D"Kalman filter">Kalman filters</a>).<sup id=3D"cite_ref=
-Stochastic_temporal_models_97-2" class=3D"reference"><a href=3D"https://en=
.wikipedia.org/wiki/Artificial_intelligence#cite_note-Stochastic_temporal_m=
odels-97"><span class=3D"cite-bracket">[</span>91<span class=3D"cite-bracke=
