o" title=3D"Digital video">videos</a>, <a href=3D"https://en.wikipedia.org/=
wiki/Digital_audio" title=3D"Digital audio">audio</a>, <a href=3D"https://e=
n.wikipedia.org/wiki/Software_code" class=3D"mw-redirect" title=3D"Software=
 code">software code</a> or other forms of data.<sup id=3D"cite_ref-169" cl=
ass=3D"reference"><a href=3D"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Artificial_intel=
ligence#cite_note-169"><span class=3D"cite-bracket">[</span>159<span class=
=3D"cite-bracket">]</span></a></sup> These models <a href=3D"https://en.wik=
ipedia.org/wiki/Machine_learning" title=3D"Machine learning">learn the unde=
rlying patterns</a> and structures of their <a href=3D"https://en.wikipedia=
.org/wiki/Training_data" class=3D"mw-redirect" title=3D"Training data">trai=
ning data</a>, and use them to generate new data<sup id=3D"cite_ref-170" cl=
ass=3D"reference"><a href=3D"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Artificial_intel=
ligence#cite_note-170"><span class=3D"cite-bracket">[</span>160<span class=
=3D"cite-bracket">]</span></a></sup> in response to input, which often take=
s the form of <a href=3D"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Natural_language" ti=
tle=3D"Natural language">natural language</a> <a href=3D"https://en.wikiped=
ia.org/wiki/Prompt_(natural_language)" class=3D"mw-redirect" title=3D"Promp=
t (natural language)"><i>prompts</i></a>.<sup id=3D"cite_ref-Generative_art=
ificial_intelligence_nytimes2_171-0" class=3D"reference"><a href=3D"https:/=
/en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Artificial_intelligence#cite_note-Generative_artific=
ial_intelligence_nytimes2-171"><span class=3D"cite-bracket">[</span>161<spa=
