e_ref-FOOTNOTERussellNorvig202126_397-0" class=3D"reference"><a href=3D"htt=
ps://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Artificial_intelligence#cite_note-FOOTNOTERussel=
lNorvig202126-397"><span class=3D"cite-bracket">[</span>373<span class=3D"c=
ite-bracket">]</span></a></sup>
</p><p>AI gradually restored its reputation in the late 1990s and early 21s=
t century by exploiting formal mathematical methods and by finding specific=
 solutions to specific problems. This "<a href=3D"https://en.wikipedia.org/=
wiki/Narrow_AI" class=3D"mw-redirect" title=3D"Narrow AI">narrow</a>" and "=
formal" focus allowed researchers to produce verifiable results and collabo=
rate with other fields (such as <a href=3D"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/St=
atistics" title=3D"Statistics">statistics</a>, <a href=3D"https://en.wikipe=
dia.org/wiki/Economics" title=3D"Economics">economics</a> and <a href=3D"ht=
tps://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mathematical_optimization" title=3D"Mathematica=
l optimization">mathematics</a>).<sup id=3D"cite_ref-Formal_and_narrow_meth=
ods_adopted_in_the_1990s_398-0" class=3D"reference"><a href=3D"https://en.w=
ikipedia.org/wiki/Artificial_intelligence#cite_note-Formal_and_narrow_metho=
ds_adopted_in_the_1990s-398"><span class=3D"cite-bracket">[</span>374<span =
class=3D"cite-bracket">]</span></a></sup> By 2000, solutions developed by A=
I researchers were being widely used, although in the 1990s they were rarel=
y described as "artificial intelligence" (a tendency known as the <a href=
=3D"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/AI_effect" title=3D"AI effect">AI effect<=
/a>).<sup id=3D"cite_ref-399" class=3D"reference"><a href=3D"https://en.wik=
ipedia.org/wiki/Artificial_intelligence#cite_note-399"><span class=3D"cite-=
bracket">[</span>375<span class=3D"cite-bracket">]</span></a></sup>
However, several academic researchers became concerned that AI was no longe=
r pursuing its original goal of creating versatile, fully intelligent machi=
nes. Beginning around 2002, they founded the subfield of <a href=3D"https:/=
/en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Artificial_general_intelligence" title=3D"Artificial=
 general intelligence">artificial general intelligence</a> (or "AGI"), whic=
h had several well-funded institutions by the 2010s.<sup id=3D"cite_ref-Art=
ificial_general_intelligence_75-1" class=3D"reference"><a href=3D"https://e=
n.wikipedia.org/wiki/Artificial_intelligence#cite_note-Artificial_general_i=
ntelligence-75"><span class=3D"cite-bracket">[</span>69<span class=3D"cite-=
bracket">]</span></a></sup>
</p><p><a href=3D"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Deep_learning" title=3D"Dee=
p learning">Deep learning</a> began to dominate industry benchmarks in 2012=
 and was adopted throughout the field.<sup id=3D"cite_ref-Deep_learning_rev=
olution_13-1" class=3D"reference"><a href=3D"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/=
Artificial_intelligence#cite_note-Deep_learning_revolution-13"><span class=
=3D"cite-bracket">[</span>11<span class=3D"cite-bracket">]</span></a></sup>
For many specific tasks, other methods were abandoned.<sup id=3D"cite_ref-4=
01" class=3D"reference"><a href=3D"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Artificial=
_intelligence#cite_note-401"><span class=3D"cite-bracket">[</span>y<span cl=
ass=3D"cite-bracket">]</span></a></sup>
